# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Secrets — none of these is ever committed
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# ⚠️  The templates are excluded **one by one**.
#
#     `.env.*` above swallows everything starting with `.env.` — including the
#     template files. And an uncommitted template means the first new developer
#     does not even know the variable exists: they clone the repository and find
#     an incomplete configuration with no indication of what is missing.
!.env.public.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
secrets/
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*.zip
src.zip


